  clock: 6  # d889
  nonce: d889  # d889
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-02: owner-chosen option (e), floor with abstention. Local branch jgstern-agent/feat/motiz-floor-identity (worktree ~/hg_wt/motiz-e), based on origin/dev cb1d8bd979. NOT pushed or merged. Supersedes the rejected 41eb17ca29 (branch jgstern-agent/fix/motiz); nothing was cherry-picked from it whole.\nCOMMITS: e10f775387 test (red), 42b8b0632b feat.\nCODE (analyze/base.py): new floor_stable_id_key(kind, language, path, name) = make_declaration_stable_id(...) for a language-bearing symbol whose kind is outside _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES (None otherwise). populate_kind_stable_ids groups floor candidates by (path, floor key) and stamps only a group of one whose key no other symbol in the file already holds. Larger groups stay null, so split_within_file_stable_id_collisions never sees a floor key. Table kinds, producer values and language=None stand-ins are unchanged.\nVALIDATOR: stable_id_stats.floor_cohort and floor_abstained, recomputed from the emitted records through the same helper. docs/schema.json regenerated; VALIDATION_REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION 0.3 -> 0.4; top-level SCHEMA_VERSION not bumped. No stable_id_scheme bump.\nDOCS: ADR-0035 section 1 (the floor rule) and section 6 (scheme standing); ADR-0014 section 5b rewritten to the current 15-row path-anchored table; spec section 6 (null = the run cannot back an identity; the floor formula; the two stats).\nTESTS: red on dev, 18 failing in the red run. Mutation: stamping every floor group, which leaves the split to the occurrence pass, turns the two-run transfer tests red in core and lang-common (elixir: the line-3 clause took the deleted line-2 clause's id; proto: B's Inner took A's Inner's id). The code was restored afterwards. Targeted smart-test on the board: 22327 passed, 1 skipped, 4 xfailed, 0 failed (752 files); the changed source files are at 100% coverage; the mypy ratchet is clean (503/503).\nMEASURED (dev cb1d8bd979 vs branch, samples copied from ~/whole_bunch_of_repos; the node-id sets are identical; 0 dev non-null values changed; 0 values became null):\n- cowboy/src: none_cohort 697 -> 0; floor_cohort 697; floor_abstained 0.\n- phoenix/lib: none_cohort 1621 -> 699; floor_cohort 922; floor_abstained 699 (elixir function 672, macro 27).\n- envoy/api/envoy/config: none_cohort 561 -> 4; floor_cohort 557; floor_abstained 4.\n- Ids equal to an :occ:<n> rehash of their own floor key (emission-order ids): 0 on all three samples. Instrument control: the rejected 41eb17ca29 tree scores 441 on phoenix and 2 on envoy.\n- Live two-run delete-a-sibling fixture (delete proto message A, service S and the first elixir greet clause): dev 0 ids moved (everything null); 41eb17ca29 4 ids moved onto another symbol; branch 0 moved, 2 null->value (B's Inner, T's Get).\nNOT CHECKED: the self-map; any full repository; the ADR-0057 SCIP merge path run live (opt-in; read only); whether nested class names in the factory table have the same missing-scope weakness. Residual for the ambiguous groups: re-scope proposed on WI-tusad-rilub-jipuv-tibum-rijab-tahut-kijov-toral."  # d889
