- op: discuss  # 4403
  at: '2026-10-02T07:07:11Z'  # 4403
  by: agent  # 4403
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4403
  clock: 8  # 4403
  nonce: '4403'  # 4403
  message: "DONE: merged in PR #1390, built as the owner-chosen option (e) from motiz_review.md (the earlier commit 41eb17ca29 was NOT merged: it gave emission-order ids that moved between symbols). populate_kind_stable_ids gives a language-bearing symbol of a kind outside the factory table the floor key sha256(kind:language:path:name) ONLY when that key is unique among the file's floor candidates (and no other symbol in the file holds it); otherwise its stable_id stays null. The occurrence index never splits a floor key. Validator stable_id_stats gains floor_cohort and floor_abstained (validation_report schema 0.3 -> 0.4). ADR-0035 s1 states the rule (s6: no stable_id scheme bump, per the owner, also for a later producer value replacing a floor value); ADR-0014 s5b rewritten to the current 15-row table; spec s6 says a null means the run cannot back an identity.\nBehavioural evidence: two-run delete-a-sibling tests (proto nested message A / service S, elixir clause) -- surviving ids are unchanged or null, never a deleted sibling's; a mutation restoring the rejected fill-everything behaviour turns both red. Samples dev -> branch: cowboy/src erlang nulls 697 -> 0; phoenix/lib elixir 1621 -> 699 (922 floor ids, 699 abstained); envoy config proto 561 -> 4. Node-id sets identical; no existing value changed; 0 emission-order ids (the rejected tree scores 441 on phoenix). Targeted smart-test 22327 passed / 0 failed.\nNOT asserted: no symbol is ever null (ambiguous same-name groups abstain by design: WI-tusad, re-scope proposed there with P2 recommended; elixir arity resolves only 84 of 250 null groups on phoenix). Not checked: rust-analyzer merge path where SCIP carries an id and tree-sitter takes the floor. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/motiz_e.md"  # 4403
